sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila kikkawai Turing wavelength at 2.3 µm (detail, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 82.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg activator-substrate kinetics on a 46.86 µm periodic patch, with inhibitor diffusivity set so the linear growth-rate peak is 2.344 µm (campaign detail scale 2.343e-06 m, Holocene 0 Ma). A single-mode PDE growth assay tracks that peak across five diffusivities at Pearson r = 0.9993. The saturated hero field that is drawn, however, has a radial FFT wavelength of 2.182 µm (6.9% short of 2.343 µm). Chronoseries at the same a, b, Du: D. mauritiana 1.820 µm, D. kikkawai 2.344 µm, D. hydei 3.056 µm. GIF 12 frames at 640×480, cv_sim_similarity 94.4 against the pinned gallery plate. Wikimedia Commons had no species photograph. Overall 82.9/100 (faithfulness 81.6, reproducibility 86.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-kikkawai-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 2318215 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 cf30dcbbcfa9c3cfb699c06488b06ce1df87d2f1c184dfeba73556f931dd350c (sha256 cf30dcbbcfa9c3cfb699c06488b06ce1df87d2f1c184dfeba73556f931dd350c), spec_fingerprint dab1edfd3ce2230430dac30458215ff2efe58254b8b6a2e95b6d00930fe73df6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dab1edfd3ce2230430dac30458215ff2efe58254b8b6a2e95b6d00930fe73df6; artifact_sha256: cf30dcbbcfa9c3cfb699c06488b06ce1df87d2f1c184dfeba73556f931dd350c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_kikkawai_specimen.jpg=1025334f37e7770a..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=45a01a384a7d9fe1..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=37400061d5790447..., datasets/drosophila_kikkawai_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=cfe6e4b2724a3595...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) showed a reaction-diffusion system can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the activator-substrate kinetics used here. | Gibert, Moreteau & David (1999) showed abdominal pigmentation in D. kikkawai depends on a major gene interacting with sex, segment, and temperature. Yassin et al. (2016) identified pdm3 as a hotspot for female-limited colour dimorphism in Drosophila.; reconstructed_in_script: The 2.343 µm length is the MorphoEval detail-tier assignment for slot 3190, realised as the Schnakenberg growth-rate peak at Du=0.020, Dv=1.364, a=0.070, b=0.940. | Predecessor D. hydei (Dv=4.470, λ≈3.056 µm) and successor D. mauritiana (Dv=0.413, λ≈1.820 µm) differ only in inhibitor range. The light/dark major-gene axis is reconstructed as b=0.710 versus b=1.180.; transfer_boundary: The ordering is a property of this dispersion relation at 0 Ma. It is not a measured fossil or morphometric series, and it does not transfer to the 93 µm tergite-band slot.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Gibert et al. or Yassin et al. measured a 2.3 µm pigment wavelength. | Does not claim the gallery plate is a light micrograph of that carrier. Commons returned no D. kikkawai photograph on 2026-10-27. | Does not claim the saturated hero field's FFT peak (2.182 µm) already equals the linear prediction. That gap is remediation R1.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': \"Seed the hero activator on Fourier mode m=20 so the rendered field's radial FFT wavelength lies within 3% of 2.343 µm. Pass 1 measures 2.182 µm on that field.\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Put the corrected hero wavelength in the comparison-figure title and keep the pure field visible beside the plate.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Re-run image fitness after the retune. cv_sim_similarity must stay at or above 58 and the GIF must stay at least 12 frames and 480 px.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Record signing as unavailable if ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is still absent. Do not invent a trusty URI.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.829"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

